(module token)

;; driver-spec.txt section 10, Exclusive-Edit Tokens. Per-step AND
;; single-threaded. The closure to a whole wave is NOT a trace induction,
;; which is what this comment said until 4e.
;;
;; token-during proves a PHASE-INDEXED INVARIANT, not an ordering. The body
;; is a three-case match over a nullary Phase and both posts are guarded
;; implications over a single arm each; nothing here expresses a sequence, a
;; transition, or a pair of phases. So a memoryless function of the current
;; phase yields the whole-wave property POINTWISE once the labelling is
;; granted. What is missing is therefore not an induction over fills but the
;; labelling itself: a refinement mapping from the driver's states onto this
;; Phase, which is a fact about the port rather than a theorem about this
;; module, and is not Lean-dischargeable.
;;
;; SINGLE-THREADED is part of the claim and not a throughput note. The
;; labelling is a function only while at most one hole is live; with two live
;; holes one driver state carries two phases and the mapping stops being one.
;; The serial wave is a PRECONDITION of the abstraction.

(type Phase (| AgentWorking) (| Briefing) (| Submitting))
(type TokenState (| Released) (| Held))

(def token-during [p: Phase] -> TokenState
  (post (=> (= p AgentWorking) (= result Released))
    :source "[S10-NOTHELD] driver-spec.txt sec 10 - a token MUST NOT be held while an agent is working")
  (post (=> (= p Submitting) (= result Held))
    :source "[S10-FRESH] driver-spec.txt sec 10 - obtain a fresh token at the moment of submission")
  (match p
    ((AgentWorking) Released)
    ((Briefing) Held)
    ((Submitting) Held)))
